# panic_recursion_report — RUNTIME trap test (WS1-131, §1K). `loopRec` recurses
# with no base case. A statically-recursive operation is instrumented with a
# depth guard: each entry bumps a shared counter, and past the limit (10000) the
# guard fires `ss_panic` with SSR0013 and exits 134 — a structured runaway-
# recursion report that fires (for small frames) before the native stack guard
# would, instead of an opaque stack-overflow crash. Legitimate bounded recursion
# (e.g. factorial, depth 5) is far under the limit and unaffected.
#
# Correctness observation (verified): the program compiles and runs, then traps
# with `EAV PANIC SSR0013 recursion-depth-exceeded` naming the op, row, reason,
# and operands (depth=10001, limit=10000); the process exits 134.
# Expected: runtime panic SSR0013 (recursion-depth-exceeded), exit 134.

PanicRecursionReport is project
PanicRecursionReport module examplesPanicRecursionReport
PanicRecursionReport target console
PanicRecursionReport entry main

examplesPanicRecursionReport is module
examplesPanicRecursionReport path examples.panicRecursionReport
examplesPanicRecursionReport exports main
examplesPanicRecursionReport purpose "Trip the recursion-depth guard and report it"
examplesPanicRecursionReport invariant "Traps via ss_panic before overflowing the stack"

ExitCode is alias
ExitCode for Int32
ExitCode purpose "Process exit status"

main is operation
main out ExitCode
main async no
main purpose "Start an unbounded recursion and trip the ss_panic depth guard"
main invariant "Never completes: panics at runtime with SSR0013"
main let seed immutable Int64 0
main let okCode immutable ExitCode 0
main do recCall
main return okCode

recCall is call
recCall in main
recCall invokes loopRec
recCall arg n Int64 seed
recCall out result Int64

loopRec is operation
loopRec in n Int64
loopRec out Int64
loopRec purpose "Recurse with no base case to drive the depth counter past its limit"
loopRec invariant "Tail-recurses unconditionally; bounded only by the WS1-131 guard"
loopRec do selfCall
loopRec return deeper

selfCall is call
selfCall in loopRec
selfCall invokes loopRec
selfCall arg n Int64 n
selfCall out deeper Int64
